hypotheses.statement:
Let $Y=\prod_{j=1}^s\mathbb P^{a_j}$, where $a_j\ge0$ and $M=\sum_j a_j\ge1$. For each $1\le\ell\le M$, let $F_\ell$ be a multihomogeneous polynomial of degree one in two distinct coordinate groups, indexed by $u_\ell,v_\ell$, and degree zero in the other groups. Any finite collection of distinct simple common zeros of these equations has size at most $$\label{polar:product-coefficient}
 [H_1^{a_1}\cdots H_s^{a_s}]
       \prod_{\ell=1}^M(H_{u_\ell}+H_{v_\ell}).$$ Other zeros and components of any dimension are allowed.

Let $N,n,\mu\ge1$ and $h\ge0$ be integers. Suppose that $P\in\mathbb C[x_1,\ldots,x_N]$ is a coefficientwise limit of determinants of $n\times n$ matrices of affine-linear forms. Let $\Psi:\mathbb C^{h+1}\to\mathbb C^N$ be an affine map and $w_1,\ldots,w_h\in\mathbb C^N$ constant directions. If $$\label{polar:affine-certificate}
 P(\Psi(\xi))=0,\qquad
 (\partial_{w_i}P)(\Psi(\xi))=0\quad(1\le i\le h)$$ has at least $\mu$ distinct simple zeros, then $$\begin{aligned}
 \mu&\le [H^{h+1}U^{n-1}V^{n-1}]
            (H+U)^n(H+V)^{n-1}(U+V)^h\label{polar:ambient-coefficient}\\
  &\le 2^h\binom{2n-1}{h+1},\notag\\
 n&\ge\frac{h+1}{4e}\mu^{1/(h+1)}.\label{polar:ambient-size}
\end{aligned}$$ The binomial coefficient is zero if $h+1>2n-1$.

